README.OSK -- how MNews and nn build on this diskThis directory is Ulrich Dessauer's MNews package exactly as its archivecarried it (the Microware OS-9 archive's APPS/mnews.t.Z), with onefile changed and its original kept beside it, as the package's owncopyright asks: changed sources travel with the originals.  NN_OSK/term.c      one line added: an `#endif' closing the `#ifdef                     HAVE_TERMIO' at line 348, which the file as                     distributed never closes.  Microware's cpp stops on                     it ("missing #endif").  NN_OSK/term.c.ori is the                     original.Everything else builds as it came.  What the build needs:  * TOP's os9lib: its library (GNULIB/os9lib.l) and its headers    (DEFS/os9lib), which the package was written against -- getgecos(),    the SysInfo calls, os9lib's own stat.h.  * Henry Spencer's regexp.h, which is NN_OSK/regexp.h; the functions    are in os9lib.l.  * strdup() and vsprintf(), from SRC/unixlib.  * error_log(), which the makefile expected from TOP's err.l.  No    archive here carries err.l, so the rebuild driver supplies a    one-function stand-in that writes the message to standard error.The makefiles install into /h0/ETC/CMDS, and inews, rnews, sbatch andnn look for one another there; the spool and library directories areset in config.h and NN_OSK/config.h.  At run time every program readsthe SysInfo data module -- TOP's system information table, which`setup' builds from a text file -- for the host name, the newsdirectories and its locks.